drm: a Kconfig entry that builds in the helpers kstb-drm needs

kstb-drm (linux/drivers/kstb-drm.c) is an external module, so it can't select
the hidden DRM helper symbols itself. DRM_KSTB selects them: DMA GEM, KMS
helpers and the in-kernel clients (fbdev emulation for the console).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/Kconfig
@@ -215,3 +215,14 @@
 	  * 4.40" Sharp Memory LCD (LS044Q7DH01)
 
 	  If M is selected the module will be called sharp_memory.
+
+config DRM_KSTB
+	bool "Helpers for the KSTB6077 display driver (an external module)"
+	depends on DRM && OF
+	select DRM_CLIENT_SELECTION
+	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
+	select DRM_KMS_HELPER
+	help
+	  kstb-drm, the KSTB6077's HDMI display driver, is built outside the
+	  tree (linux/drivers/kstb-drm.c). This builds the DRM helpers it uses
+	  (DMA GEM, KMS, fbdev emulation) into the kernel.
